## 4. Controlling Output File Count

The **small files problem** is one of the most common production issues.

```python
# Bad: 1000s of tiny files (one per Spark partition)
df.write.parquet("s3://bucket/output/")

# Good: Control output file count
df.coalesce(20).write.parquet("s3://bucket/output/")

# Best for partitioned data: one file per partition key
df.repartition("date") \
  .write \
  .partitionBy("date") \
  .parquet("s3://bucket/output/")
```

### Writing a Single File (reports/exports)

```python
df.coalesce(1).write \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .option("header", "true") \
    .csv("s3://bucket/reports/daily_summary/")
# ⚠️ coalesce(1) brings all data to one executor — only for small DataFrames
```

