## 5. Saving as Tables vs Paths

```python
# Write to a path (raw files)
df.write.parquet("s3://bucket/raw/orders/")

# Write as a managed table (Hive metastore / Glue catalog)
df.write.saveAsTable("orders")  # Spark manages location

# Write as an external table (you manage location)
df.write \
    .option("path", "s3://bucket/raw/orders/") \
    .saveAsTable("orders_external")

# Write using SQL-style
df.createOrReplaceTempView("orders_temp")
spark.sql("CREATE TABLE orders AS SELECT * FROM orders_temp")
```

