## 7. Production-Grade Write Pattern

```python
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession

spark = SparkSession.builder \
    .appName("OrdersIngestion") \
    .config("spark.sql.sources.partitionOverwriteMode", "dynamic") \
    .config("spark.sql.parquet.compression.codec", "snappy") \
    .getOrCreate()

def write_partitioned_data(df, output_path: str, partition_cols: list):
    """
    Production-safe partitioned write with dynamic overwrite.
    Overwrites only affected partitions, leaves others untouched.
    """
    df.repartition(*partition_cols) \
      .write \
      .mode("overwrite") \
      .partitionBy(*partition_cols) \
      .option("maxRecordsPerFile", 500_000) \
      .option("compression", "snappy") \
      .parquet(output_path)

# Usage
write_partitioned_data(
    df=orders_df,
    output_path="s3://bucket/processed/orders/",
    partition_cols=["year", "month"]
)
```

